<article class="env-lemma" id="0E2D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E2D">Lemma <span data-tag="0E2D">47.27.2</span>.</a> Let $R \to A$ be a flat ring map of finite presentation. Any two relative dualizing complexes for $R \to A$ are isomorphic. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $K$ and $L$ be two relative dualizing complexes for $R \to A$. Denote $K_1 = K \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} (A \otimes _ R A)$ and $L_2 = (A \otimes _ R A) \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} L$ the derived base changes via the first and second coprojections $A \to A \otimes _ R A$. By symmetry the assumption on $L_2$ implies that $R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{A \otimes _ R A}(A, L_2)$ is isomorphic to $A$. By More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0ATK" data-tag="0ATK">15.100.3</a> part (3) applied twice we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  A \otimes _{A \otimes _ R A}^\mathbf {L} L_2 \cong R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{A \otimes _ R A}(A, K_1 \otimes _{A \otimes _ R A}^\mathbf {L} L_2) \cong A \otimes _{A \otimes _ R A}^\mathbf {L} K_1  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Applying the restriction functor $D(A \otimes _ R A) \to D(A)$ for either coprojection we obtain the desired result. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>